{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat ../research.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"audit_spec_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-03_13-18-41-etcd_raft-real-run/audit-spec/v2.json\",\n  \"audit_spec_version\": 2,\n  \"activity_roles\": {\n    \"A1\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Qualified support for decision formation and legal advancement\"\n    },\n    \"A2\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Context validity and acquisition, transfer or loss of authority\"\n    },\n    \"A3\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Recovery and resynchronization of eligible participation\"\n    },\n    \"A4\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Configuration and participant eligibility\"\n    },\n    \"A5\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Decision application and consumption\"\n    },\n    \"A6\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"History, persistence and reconstruction of support\"\n    },\n    \"A7\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Client contracts, invocation intervals and observed completion\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"activity_focus\": [],\n  \"understanding_status\": \"usable\",\n  \"core_overview\": {\n    \"formation\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Leader proposals receive term/index, append to the log and queue a persistence-delayed self acknowledgment. Peer acknowledgments update progress; tracker aggregates current voters using both majorities for joint configuration, then maybeCommit checks the current log term before advancing commitment. Acknowledgment-driven advancement broadcasts append and releases queued reads, while configuration-driven advancement broadcasts without that release. Voter sets use n/2+1 majorities. Followers match the preceding entry, protect committed history and publish durable append responses. Rejection probes, heartbeat recovery and snapshots replenish lagging support. Ready delivers committed entries separately from actual host application.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"b-commit\",\n        \"b-ready\",\n        \"b-recovery\",\n        \"b-application\",\n        \"b-membership\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"f-current-term-commit\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-commit-reset\",\n        \"s-response-commit\",\n        \"s-config\",\n        \"s-tracker-commit\",\n        \"s-joint\",\n        \"s-majority\",\n        \"s-log-start-append\",\n        \"s-send-repair\",\n        \"s-log-apply\",\n        \"s-node-contract\",\n        \"s-log-commit\",\n        \"s-ready\",\n        \"s-ready-accept\",\n        \"s-advance\",\n        \"s-send\",\n        \"s-host-contract\",\n        \"s-async-contract\",\n        \"s-ready-contract\",\n        \"s-raw-api\",\n        \"s-async-build\",\n        \"s-async-config\",\n        \"s-node-loop\",\n        \"s-node-step\",\n        \"s-storage-complete\",\n        \"s-restore\",\n        \"s-role-handlers\",\n        \"s-log-advance\",\n        \"s-applied-followup\",\n        \"s-config-changer\",\n        \"s-config-restore\",\n        \"s-proposal-read\",\n        \"s-restart\",\n        \"s-load-state\",\n        \"s-read-result\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Campaign transitions establish candidate term and self vote; vote eligibility uses local vote/leader context and log freshness. PreVote leaves term and vote unchanged. Step handles message terms before role handlers, with explicit pre-vote/lease exceptions and lower-term rejection. Role reset clears accumulated progress and readOnly context while preserving the committed prefix. Candidate handlers accept the matching vote response kind, deduplicate votes and tally current voters. Pre-vote success starts an actual campaign; real quorum success elects a leader and appends its no-op. Timer quorum loss and higher terms revoke leadership; transfer waits for target replication and expires. Campaign admission excludes learners, pending snapshots and committed configuration entries above the accounted applied frontier.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"b-context\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"f-applied-frontier\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-authority\",\n        \"s-campaign\",\n        \"s-term\",\n        \"s-voting\",\n        \"s-commit-reset\",\n        \"s-role-handlers\",\n        \"s-vote-tally\",\n        \"s-timers\",\n        \"s-campaign-guard\",\n        \"s-promotable\",\n        \"s-majority\",\n        \"s-check-quorum\",\n        \"s-active-quorum\",\n        \"s-log-start-append\",\n        \"s-log-advance\",\n        \"s-node-contract\",\n        \"s-ready-accept\",\n        \"s-advance\",\n        \"s-restart\",\n        \"s-applied-followup\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Term dispatch prevents ordinary old responses from becoming new leader support. Persistence-delayed vote/append replies and leader self replies connect durable support to election and commit decisions. Configuration application reinterprets peer progress through a changed voter set and may itself advance commitment; established committed history constrains snapshots and subsequent log repair. Host configuration installation changes voter eligibility separately from application accounting. Restart restores term/vote, committed history and ConfState, while volatile support is rebuilt. Async storage uses FIFO completion and term-stamped append responses; application acknowledgments remain term-independent. Old pre-first-commit read requests can survive a reset, but read quorum acknowledgments do not; any later release uses current committed state and a fresh read round. Synchronous early Advance can account application before external completion, leaving configuration admission timing as a focused unresolved premise.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"b-context\",\n        \"b-ready\",\n        \"b-commit\",\n        \"b-membership\",\n        \"b-application\",\n        \"b-reconstruction\",\n        \"b-read\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"f-applied-frontier\",\n        \"f-current-term-commit\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-term\",\n        \"s-send\",\n        \"s-config\",\n        \"s-restore\",\n        \"s-async-build\",\n        \"s-node-contract\",\n        \"s-restart\",\n        \"s-config-restore\",\n        \"s-read-state\",\n        \"s-read-release\",\n        \"s-authority\",\n        \"s-campaign\",\n        \"s-voting\",\n        \"s-commit-reset\",\n        \"s-role-handlers\",\n        \"s-vote-tally\",\n        \"s-majority\",\n        \"s-timers\",\n        \"s-check-quorum\",\n        \"s-active-quorum\",\n        \"s-campaign-guard\",\n        \"s-promotable\",\n        \"s-ready\",\n        \"s-ready-accept\",\n        \"s-advance\",\n        \"s-host-contract\",\n        \"s-async-contract\",\n        \"s-ready-contract\",\n        \"s-raw-api\",\n        \"s-async-config\",\n        \"s-node-loop\",\n        \"s-node-step\",\n        \"s-storage-complete\",\n        \"s-response-commit\",\n        \"s-log-commit\",\n        \"s-tracker-commit\",\n        \"s-joint\",\n        \"s-config-changer\",\n        \"s-proposal-read\",\n        \"s-log-apply\",\n        \"s-log-advance\",\n        \"s-applied-followup\",\n        \"s-log-start-append\",\n        \"s-load-state\",\n        \"s-storage-contract\",\n        \"s-memory-storage\",\n        \"s-bootstrap\",\n        \"s-read-contract\",\n        \"s-read-ack\",\n        \"s-read-result\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"Pending-read release following configuration-driven first current-term commit.\",\n      \"Synchronous persistence/send ordering discrepancy across interface descriptions.\",\n      \"Whether early synchronous Advance may precede configuration installation and allow campaigning with stale membership.\",\n      \"Flow-control limits, all snapshot overlap histories and optional lease clock assumptions are not exhaustively investigated.\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Representative formation, authority, old-work, configuration, persistence, recovery and consumption paths are now traced. Local contract and scheduling uncertainties remain explicit and do not prevent focused investigation.\"\n  },\n  \"understanding_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"abda8828f7a848e49d21c51418958ef0\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"abda8828f7a848e49d21c51418958ef0\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"a4567a01174c47be8a79a362d2e10330\",\n      \"version\": 2,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"a4567a01174c47be8a79a362d2e10330\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"next_objective\": {\n    \"action\": \"investigate_and_refocus\",\n    \"boundary\": \"both_core_paths\",\n    \"reason\": \"Use results to update understanding and compare the remaining frontier\",\n    \"core_gaps\": []\n  },\n  \"drafts\": [],\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cc41ebdc8ff24f87be8731a39b2069b1\",\n      \"question\": {\n        \"audit_spec_version\": 2,\n        \"disposition\": \"needs_specific_evidence\",\n        \"preferred_check\": \"source_review\",\n        \"question\": \"Does the synchronous Node.Advance optimization permit advancing a Ready containing a committed configuration change before ApplyConfChange, and if so can the accounted applied frontier let that node campaign using superseded membership?\",\n        \"importance\": \"If permitted overlap